<div class="page-head">
  <div><h1>Bulk import</h1><p>Load many items at once from Excel or CSV. New items import as drafts so you can check them before publishing.</p></div>
  <a class="btn" href="/backend/import/template.csv"><%- icon('download') %>Download CSV template</a>
</div>
<div class="split">
  <form class="card" method="post" action="/backend/import" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <h2 class="h3">Upload a file</h2>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="file">Excel (.xlsx) or CSV file, up to 5 MB</label>
      <input id="file" type="file" name="file" accept=".xlsx,.csv,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet,text/csv" required>
      <div class="hint">The VaayuTrip rate card (Hotels, Activities, Transfers and Currency tabs) is read as it is. Any other Excel file or CSV must use the columns on the right.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="country">Country for cities we don't recognise <span class="muted">(optional)</span></label>
      <select id="country" name="country">
        <option value="">Work it out from the file</option>
        <% countries.forEach(c => { %><option><%= c %></option><% }) %>
      </select>
      <div class="hint">Used when a row only has a city we have no inventory in yet, e.g. a new city in Vietnam.</div>
    </div>
    <button class="btn btn-primary">Import</button>
    <div class="alert info" style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:13px;display:block">
      <b>Rate card notes</b>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:18px">
        <li>Costs in AED, USD, IDR… are converted to ₹ with the rates on the Currency tab (it must include INR). They are VaayuTrip's costs: agents see them plus VaayuTrip's margin (Admin → Settings).</li>
        <li>Hotels: one item per room, season and meal plan. Extra-bed charges are added to that hotel's description.</li>
        <li>Uploading the card again updates the rates of matching items (same city and name; for hotels also room, meal plan and season), including live ones.</li>
        <li>Per-km transfers are not imported yet.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </form>
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="h3">Columns (CSV or a single-sheet Excel)</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px">The first row must be the header. Column order doesn't matter; unknown columns are ignored.</p>
    <table class="table" style="font-size:13px">
      <colgroup><col style="width:34%"><col></colgroup>
      <tr><td><code>kind</code></td><td><%= Object.keys(kinds).join(', ') %></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>title</code>, <code>city</code></td><td>Required</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>country</code></td><td>One of: <%= countries.join(', ') %></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>category</code></td><td><% Object.entries(kinds).forEach(([k, c]) => { %><b><%= k %>:</b> <%= c.categories.join(', ') %><br><% }) %></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>price_basis</code></td><td><%= Object.keys(basisLabels).join(', ') %> (hotels are always per_room_night)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>net_adult</code></td><td>What VaayuTrip pays, in ₹: per adult, per group, or per room per night. Agents see it plus VaayuTrip's margin.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>net_child</code>, <code>net_infant</code></td><td>Optional, per-person items only</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>highlights</code>, <code>inclusions</code>, <code>exclusions</code></td><td>Separate lines with <code>|</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Kind details</td><td><%= detailColumns.map(c => c).join(', ') %></td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
